<title>UK: Societe Generale adds $60 million to perpetual FRN.</title>
<headline>Societe Generale adds $60 million to perpetual FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following floating-rate issue, has been increased by $60 million to $310 million, joint lead managers Morgan Stanley International, Bear Stearns and Societe</p>
<p>Generale said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SOCIETE GENERALE</p>
<p> AMT    *$310 MLN     BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY ***PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN   **62.50     PAY DATE    23.DEC.96</p>
<p> LAST MOODY AA3	 ISS PRICE  99.883    FULL FEES   0.75</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A	   REOFFER    =</p>
<p> NOTES	*FUNGIBLE WITH $250 MLN LAUNCHED 10.OCT.96</p>
<p>	     **FOR 10-YEARS THEN STEPS UP TO 200 BP</p>
<p>	    ***CALL FROM OCT 2006 AT PAR</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS US/UK/FR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.60	SELL CONC  0.15	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
